            "review_title": "Review at Viet Emotion Cafe Restaurant",
            "review_text": "vincentlau\nSingapore, Singapore318 contributions\n0\nSimple Restaurant but so full of Flavours\nDec 2019 • Family\nSimple, nice, clean restaurant decorated in a traditional style. Cheerful and responsive service but the food....\n\nWe ordered;\n1) Sapa Steamboat with local pork. The soup base is so addictive, hot, sourish, tinge of spiciness from the local cadammon, ginger etc...amazing soup that is so full of flavour in the cold mountain air.\n2) The fried rice is a dish of superb mastery of the wok...full of smoky flavours...\n3) The grilled pork with lemongrass...nice and sweet but would hv orderedit with onions next time cos somehow dont like the stark stalks of lemongrass\n4) Strangely the pizza was also nice and flavourful.\n\nFor a nondescript restaurant, this turned out to be a crouching tiger hidden dragon in these mountains.\nRead more\nWritten December 21, 2019",
