            "review_title": "Review at Viet Emotion Cafe Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Jobo\n9 contributions\n0\nDecent food, not authentic Vietnamese food though\nOct 2019 • Solo\nOrdered the fried tofu with tomatoes and without onions per my request - it was tasty but nothing special, light flavor which isn’t a bad or good thing - depends on the consumer. The menu said mushroom sauce but I didn’t taste any in my dish. Likely geared towards foreigners since my Vietnamese mom usually uses some fish sauce for added flavor. I would recommend it if you’re looking for something simple and satisfying but not authentic.\n\nI also got the young coconut drink which was served at room temperature although maybe they can’t refrigerate every coconut. \n\nI wanted Vietnamese bread on the side but they don’t have it available which is a poor sign of a Vietnamese restaurant. \n\nPrices are definitely made for tourists but it’s convenient to the train station and you can sit for awhile.\nRead more\nWritten October 6, 2019",
